  "caption": "Quinn reached for the seatbelt and the shoulder said no. Weeks later the arm was stuck at half-mast, jumpers were a team sport, and nights were achy.\n\nFrozen shoulder is an irritated, tightened joint capsule that moves through painful, stiff and thawing stages. It's more common with diabetes and after the arm has been kept still. Complete rest isn't the answer.\n\nWhat can help: matching care to the stage, avoiding aggressive stretching in the painful phase, tailored hands-on care and staged exercise, keeping the rest of your body training, and asking your GP about a blood sugar check if you've never had one.\n\nGet it properly assessed if there's severe, constant night pain or pain after a sudden injury.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
